Available commands:
  core:
        help        | show this help
        clear       | clears the terminal screen
        exit        | closes this terminal
        quit        | closes this program
        reload      | reloads the cartridge
        version     | reports this binary's compiled configuration
        configure   | configures terminal behaviour and appearance
        status      | reports this instance's identity and configuration
  engine:
        echo        | prints text
        metrics     | reports frame timing and the recorded metric series
        vsync       | reports or sets the presentation throttle (vsync [0|1])
        log         | tails recent log lines into this console (log [N])
        web         | transfers a URL through the declared web reach (web <url> [body])
        instances   | lists peer instances or sends one a line (instances [send <pid> <line>])
        topics      | lists the pub/sub topics or peeks one (topics [peek <name>])
        window      | reports or sets the window (window [report|size <w>x<h>|fullscreen [on|off]])
        screenshot  | captures the next frame to a file (screenshot <path>)
  debug:
        target      | aims the drive commands at a document
        click       | synthesizes a press/release arc on a widget
        doubleclick | synthesizes two arcs inside the double window
        press       | presses a point on a widget and holds it standing
        release     | puts the standing press down, travelling first if told
        ask         | the off-hand still press on a node or a board spot
        drag        | presses on a widget and pulls to another or an offset
        wheel       | turns the wheel over a widget, with or without control
        key         | feeds one composed key to the target document
        type        | types text into the target document
        read        | reads a widget's compiled rect and text
        dialog      | raises the engine file dialog for driving

Additional information might be available using "'command' --help"
